    {
      "id": "19297",
      "key": "SFCC-804",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to be able to opt in to Zimmermann marketing communications when completing a purchase via express checkout methods, so that I do not miss the opportunity to sign up regardless of which payment method I use.\\n\\nThis story was raised during the cart design call on 25th August 2026 with Emma, Rebecca, Keira, and Izzy.\\n\\nThe standard cart page includes a marketing opt-in checkbox (see SFCC-325) which allows Shoppers to sign up for marketing communications before proceeding to checkout. However, customers who use Apple Pay Express or Google Pay Express bypass the standard cart and checkout flow entirely — meaning they never see the marketing opt-in checkbox and Zimmermann has no opportunity to capture their marketing preference.\\n\\nThis enhancement covers two open questions that need to be resolved before a solution can be designed and built:\\n\\n1. How should marketing preferences be captured for Apple Pay Express and Google Pay Express customers who bypass the standard checkout flow?\\n2. Is there an alternative touchpoint (e.g. post-purchase confirmation, account creation nudge) where the marketing opt-in can be surfaced for express checkout customers?\\n\\nThis story is currently a placeholder — no solution has been agreed. Requires input from Emma/Rebecca (business requirements), Keira (UX design), and Tim (technical feasibility) before ACs can be written.\\n\\nDepends on SFCC-325 (Cart Page – Marketing Opt-In Checkbox) and SFCC-383/SFCC-384 (Apple Pay Express and Google Pay Express buttons).\\n\\nNote: this may also have implications for GDPR/privacy compliance depending on the solution — legal sign-off may be required.\""
    }
  ]
}"}

